WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.230
I came to you very care.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:08.210
Fully about two weeks ago, and I told you,
if you compared the polls today.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.120
Now, this was like August 20th.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:15.679
I said to you on August 20th, if you compare
the polls today to the polls four years ago

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:20.080
between Joe Biden I'm sorry, between Hillary
Clinton and Donald Trump, there was only a

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.590
zero point, seven point difference over that
four year period.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:30.839
And what I said on August 20th was I wouldn't
be super confident with a polling difference

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:36.579
of zero point seven points when we compare
2016 to 2020.

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:42.329
We now have another two weeks of polling data
and we now have a different situation.

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:49.219
Joe Biden today is in a different position
than that in which Hillary Clinton found herself

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:50.829
four years ago today.

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:52.890
So let's look at the numbers.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.140
Then we'll talk about the significance.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:01:00.371
Then we'll look at states right now, on average,
according to Real Clear Politics, Joe Biden

00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:04.440
is leading Donald Trump nationally by seven
point one.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.040
Now, this is an average.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.900
There are recent polls where Biden is only
up by two.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.140
The latest Emmerson poll is one example.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.150
There are polls where Biden is up by 10.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:17.010
Like the recent CBS YouGov poll, the latest
USC poll.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:22.270
But on average, Biden is up seven point one,
OK?

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:29.370
On this day in 2016, meaning September 8th,
2016, Hillary Clinton was leading Donald Trump

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.560
by only 2.8 percent.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.570
This is now a different situation.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:39.790
If you go back four years, Hillary Clinton's
lead was significantly smaller than that of

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:40.790
Joe Biden today.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.250
Now, what does this mean?

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.710
Nothing, nothing.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:44.710
Nothing.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:45.710
Everyone must vote.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:52.160
It is simply interesting to consider that
as of today, Joe Biden's lead is 2.5 times

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.430
that of Hillary Clinton.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:56.300
Exactly four years ago.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:02.000
What are the odds that if Trump loses by seven,
he wins the Electoral College?

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.390
They are low, but unless we vote, it means
nothing.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:12.540
And of course, this is an electoral race which
will come down to a handful of states.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.599
And looking at recent polling, some highlights
from the last five days.

00:02:16.599 --> 00:02:18.829
Donald Trump is winning by five in Missouri.

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:19.829
As of yesterday.

00:02:19.829 --> 00:02:21.519
Now, why do we care about Missouri?

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:26.340
We care about Missouri because in 2016, Trump
won Missouri by 19.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.819
If Donald Trump were to win Missouri by only
five.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:30.079
That's not good for him.

00:02:30.079 --> 00:02:36.400
In Wisconsin, Biden is up eight in a right
leaning Rasmussen poll and up six in Wisconsin

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.799
in a CBS News YouGov poll that was almost
tied in 2016.

00:02:41.799 --> 00:02:46.499
Texas has Trump at only plus two, according
to the Dallas Morning News.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:50.180
Remember that in 2016, Trump won Texas by
nine.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:55.490
If Trump were to win Texas by only two, that
would be a very interesting signal about the

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:56.490
South.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.750
Joe Biden is currently up 15 in New Mexico.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.420
That would be a wild win in 2016.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.030
Hillary did win New Mexico, but only by eight.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:10.269
Of course, if Joe Biden doubles his margin
of victory in New Mexico, that would be huge.

00:03:10.269 --> 00:03:16.989
One note is in 2016, libertarian Gary Johnson
had nine in New Mexico.

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:20.829
We'll talk about the lack of Gary Johnson
in a moment.

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:25.170
We have a recent Florida poll from the Republican
Trafalgar Group, which has Trump plus three

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.459
in Florida.

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:30.180
Florida could be a fight, but we've also got
a Quinnipiac poll from Florida that has Biden

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.499
plus three.

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:38.420
Remember, Florida is likely much more important
in the path to 270 electoral votes for Donald

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.959
Trump than it is for Joe Biden.

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:43.040
Now, let me go back to what I just mentioned.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.469
Not only do we not have Gary Johnson this
year, we also don't have Jill Stein.

00:03:48.469 --> 00:03:52.519
And if you go back and look at the numbers
from 2016, Gary Johnson ended up with a little

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:55.719
over three percent of the vote in 2016 nationally.

00:03:55.719 --> 00:03:58.260
Jill Stein ended up with about one percent
of the vote.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:05.150
Jill Stein's vote alone could it could have
flipped some states from Hillary to Trump

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:10.280
and could be solely responsible for Hillary
Clinton losing and Donald Trump winning electorally.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:16.310
But with Gary Johnson not pulling three point
two percent of the vote.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.730
We also have to consider the impact of that.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:25.560
And so anybody saying the third party difference
this year is going to make it very clear that

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.500
Trump will win or Trump will lose?

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.700
I think we don't know that.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.200
I think everybody has to vote.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.080
I think we've got to count every ballot.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.080
Now, last word of warning.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.070
And this is this is maybe the most important
thing.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:43.880
The polls, as accurate as they might be about
the intentions of voters, cannot tell us the

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.660
effect of voter suppression.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.600
The polls don't tell us the effect of messing
with the postal service.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.320
The polls cannot account for voter purges
that we know are going on and have been reporting

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.320
on.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.260
And so this is the really important message.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.690
Biden today with a lead that's two and a half
time.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.910
Larger than Hillary's lead in 2016.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:04.970
That's a beautiful thing.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.350
That's a great thing.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:09.090
But it does not account for any of the foul
play.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:13.880
And if it's close, and especially if Trump
comes out ahead on election night in some

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.450
states and then the lead starts to shrink
as absentee ballots are counted in the days

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:24.040
following and it goes more and more to Joe
Biden, Donald Trump will use courts, many

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:31.590
of which are overseen by the judges he installed
to try to stop the counting of absentee ballots.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:42.000
So is 2.5 X in terms of the lead the the multiple
by which Joe Biden is leading over Hillary

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Clinton's lead?

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Good for us.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Well, yeah, it's good.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.150
But given all of these other question marks,
I would be far more comfortable if the lead

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.870
were bigger and I would be far more comfortable
if I knew we were going to absolutely crush

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:53.870
turnout.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:54.870
So the messages.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:06:36.480
We've got

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.390
to vote.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:07:03.930
We've got

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.960
to vote.

